Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Services Fail to Start After Update
Symptoms: Services show failed status after package updates

Solution:

# Check service logs
sudo journalctl -u automation-controller-web -n 50

# Reset failed services
sudo systemctl reset-failed

# Check configuration syntax
sudo nginx -t
sudo -u awx /var/lib/awx/venv/awx/bin/awx-manage check

# Restart services in correct order
sudo systemctl restart postgresql
sudo systemctl restart redis
sudo systemctl restart nginx
sudo systemctl restart automation-controller-web
Issue 2: Database Connection Issues
Symptoms: Applications cannot connect to PostgreSQL

Solution:

# Check PostgreSQL status
sudo systemctl status postgresql

# Check database logs
sudo tail -f /var/log/postgresql/postgresql-*.log

# Test database connectivity
sudo -u postgres psql -c "SELECT version();"

# Check connection limits
sudo -u postgres psql -c "SHOW max_connections;"
sudo -u postgres psql -c "SELECT count(*) FROM pg_stat_activity;"
Issue 3: High Memory Usage
Symptoms: System becomes slow, high memory consumption

Solution:

# Identify memory-consuming processes
ps aux --sort=-%mem | head -10

# Check for memory leaks in Ansible processes
sudo systemctl restart automation-controller-task

# Clear Redis cache if necessary
redis-cli FLUSHALL

# Restart services to free memory
sudo systemctl restart automation-controller-web
